From fc4c25c25ab5deb23051a7e18f30b02726d2bca8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:41:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: turn the output off and on again while its
 flips do not come

When the flip of the frame before does not come (kodi-9207), Kodi turns the
output off and on again from the second stall in a row. Whether it came on
was read from Kodi's cache of the properties of the CRTC, which holds what
Kodi asked for, and the next reset could only come a minute later, three
times while Kodi runs. nvidia-drm takes the modeset that turns the head on
and returns 0 even when it then fails to apply it ("Failed to apply atomic
modeset. Error code: -22" in the kernel log): neither the cache nor the
state of the kernel says so. That is the test of 2026-10-14, where the
display stayed without a signal: one reset, nothing logged after it, and
none again for a minute.

Whether the output is on is now read from the kernel, and what tells whether
the display came back is the flips: while they still do not come, the output
is turned off and on again after 1, 2, 4 ... 64 s (CFlipStallRecovery, which
only decides). A failure ends once flips have come for 10 s, and the next one
starts again with the short waits. Each wait spans frames: nothing loops or
blocks in one of them, and every reset is logged.
---
